# Limited installed-consumer compiler-tail scope

This is a fresh Root-only test protocol for Debug/Release × x64/Win32. It preserves production SDK and consumer source, telemetry settings, the original 4640-byte driver, the Owned client and owned-tail-evidence.cjs. This derivative selects an existing supported supervisor binary; the consumer driver, binding algorithm and policy remain the parent raw bytes. The four old capconsumer-0f35213c configure failures remain immutable inputs: they had no prelaunch tail pin and are never retroactively accepted.

Each fresh configuration retains SDK-only installation 120 s, exact CMake consumer configure 120 s, consumer-only build 600 s/parallel 2, and actual consumer runtime 30 s, all with the original 2000 ms Owned drain. The same four actual producer archives, normal generated installation scripts, 50-file package map, 34 public headers, ActionJson export/header and legal files remain bound. There is no SDK rebuild or consumer-source change. The installed CL/OBJ/LINK/project-cwd checks are the exact parent guard body.

Only configure and build have a prelaunch tailImagePin. It names the actual MSVC 14.44.35207 Hostx64 target vctip.exe disk object, fixed size/SHA and a distinct fresh nonce per stage. Existing launchOwned holds the file before root resume and existing readTailEvidence requires complete raw evidence: exact context/argv/budgets, ready/root PID and string FILETIME, prelaunch disk identity, stable exactly-one owned member, the same held process and disk object, final pre-cleanup confirmation, real signaled identity and two stable empty-Job confirmations. Snapshot errors, unknown/multiple tail, malformed evidence, missing pin, timeout, STOP, root failure, fallback or generic incomplete closure abort. No new tail names or cause/telemetry inference are permitted. These disk observations are evidence consistency, not RAM or writer authentication.

A valid exception permits subsequent finite consumer verification only. Original result.passed=false, supervisorExitCode=124, forced-owned-job flags, raw/context/stdio and terminal remain intact; receipt.accepted remains false. compileRootCompleted and compilerTailContinuation are separate finite facts. The derived preparation driver may complete its finite sequence but returns 1 whenever any generic result is false. The outer guard may continue only after this exact classification and returns 1 for the entire four-configuration run if any exception occurred. It is not acceptCompilerTail: that public policy requires Build.ps1/source-build/v2 and is not invoked here. No source-build identity or formal independent-consumer gate is invented.

Installation and runtime use the original natural-result predicate; runtime invokes the unchanged original 4640-byte driver and must genuinely close the entire Job with root/supervisor 0/0 and no force. Before runtime the guard still verifies actual installed membership and complete CL/LINK/archive/object/EXE binding, then emits a runtime plan with real artifact hashes. No future executable hashes are sealed. The original DesktopValidation lease, cleared/restored Node injection variables, Vcpkg=false and DESTDIR refusal remain unchanged.

Authored with filesystem operations only; no Node, compiler, native helper or VM executed by this author. All qualification/resource/OS/full-toolchain/release flags stay false. Future consumer evidence is pending and null; none is inferred from the old four failures or this sealed protocol.

## Supported supervisor derivative

The parent 0bea packet remains immutable. Its four installations naturally completed 0/0, but configure failed before a subject was created: stderr was Unknown option, and configure ready/owned JSONL, consumer bindings and runtime were absent. Missing subject records are not natural closure. The original 0f35213c failures also remain unchanged.

All four fresh configurations use the sealed host x64 copy at F:/work/sm05-compiler-tail/out/actual-compiler-tail-6df2df34-3e84-4f05-bffa-efbfbb555e1f/OwnedProcessRunner.exe (150016 B, SHA-256 015d0802aa62dbdbf00eca48f200d821a0f3b6a2a42896fc55ecaef3f5197bbe). Its normal build directly compiled owned-process-runner.cpp plus owned-tail-evidence.cpp. Actual CL/read, OBJ, LINK/read/write and PE x64 console bytes bind this exact executable; all three source files equal the broker versions at author time.

runner-origin.json pins the 6df2 historical actual source/tool evidence and both x64/x86 contexts/raw tails. The existing binary actually accepted image/hash/nonce and emitted start, prelaunch pin, snapshot, cleanup and terminal. Those runs kept generic passed=false, root/supervisor 0/124 and forced owned-Job cleanup; the historical 30 s drain is not this packet's unchanged 2000 ms drain. Parameter support proves neither current consumer success nor natural/resource qualification. The separate 9c838 reader failure is not used as successful evidence.

Only packet/output paths, actual supervisor path/size/SHA, eight fresh configure/build nonces and corresponding frozen control pins differ from 0bea. DELTA.json replays every modified file forward and backward to the exact original bytes. The SDK producers, install map, BinderConsumer, driver, policy, args other than fresh paths, budgets and qualification flags are preserved. This author executed filesystem operations only; future outputs remain absent.
